    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A crusading state ruled by the celibate knights of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, who conquered the pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-prussians">Prussians</a> between 1230 and about 1283.</li><li>From <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malbork-castle">Marienburg</a> the Grand Masters ran a castle-based administration and profited from Hanseatic grain and an amber monopoly.</li><li>Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-grunwald">Grunwald</a> in 1410 and the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-prussia">West Prussia</a> in 1466 broke it; in 1525 it became the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Order held a monopoly on Baltic amber, selling much of the raw amber to rosary makers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

